## Import

The `pulumi import` command can be used, for example:

Agent tokens are imported using the token ID assigned by Dagster+.
The token ID can be found via the Dagster+ API (ListAgentTokens query).
IMPORTANT: The token value (secret) is only available at creation time and
cannot be recovered after import. The <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`token`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Token`" pulumi-lang-go="`token`" pulumi-lang-python="`token`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`token`" pulumi-lang-java="`token`">`token`</span> attribute will be empty after
import — plan accordingly (e.g. use<span pulumi-lang-nodejs=" ignoreChanges " pulumi-lang-dotnet=" IgnoreChanges " pulumi-lang-go=" ignoreChanges " pulumi-lang-python=" ignore_changes " pulumi-lang-yaml=" ignoreChanges " pulumi-lang-java=" ignoreChanges "> ignoreChanges </span>or recreate the token).

